A||||11||Thor||V6 Back Three Spark Plug Problem||||9||
Z||000000||Thor||08-01-2000||12:40 AM||||All I Want to do is replace the back three spark plugs/wires on my 2.8 litre V6...The only person I know who can reach back there is my TWO YEAR OLD SON...Needless to say he's not very good with a ratchet yet.  Any one out there know a way of achieving this basic task...basiclly?...THANKS IN ADVANCE.||||reg||9
Z||000001||GT Bastard||08-01-2000||01:49 AM||||Some people think it's necessary to remove the decklid.  Makes it much easier.  I just stand in the trunk and lay over the motor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||08-01-2000||02:06 AM||||I usually place an old blanket over the trunk and engine then lay on top. My left hand goes in from the left side to guide/hold the socket and my right arm moves the ratchet handle from the top. I use a Craftsman 12" 3/8 drive flex-head ratchet.<BR>Takes me about 5 minutes to do the back side and I don't remove the decklid.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||08-01-2000||02:10 AM||||I do the same as Orief...I use a shooter's mat, lay it over the engine and trunk, and lay down and go to work.<BR> I take the decklid off though...it REALLY makes it easier, and its very simple to take off...unplug the harness on the pass side, unscrew the ground wire on drivers side, and take off the 4 bolts...its really simple and helps tremendously.<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 08-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jim's87GT||08-01-2000||07:03 AM||||I picked up a hint from another (horrors) forum that helped me.  Scratch mark the deck lid around the bracket before removing it and it will assure the correct positioning when you replace it.  It's WAY easier for me with the lid off.||||reg||7
Z||000005||Carrolles||08-01-2000||08:07 AM||||I don't remove the deck lid and it takes me about ten minutes.  Remove the engine grills and the pcv tube running from the front valve cover to the air filter housing to give a little more arm room.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ironhorse||08-01-2000||01:16 PM||||This is what I do to remove the sparkplugs, Remove the dogbone, back up a truck behind the fiero, remove dogbone, take tow strap with (wreches on it, don't know what it's call), put one end on the bumper of truck, other end on the engine (there's a bracket on the right side of the block), make the strap tighter using that wrench thingy, and VOILA I have about 5 more inches of room.||||reg||1
Z||000007||2birds||08-02-2000||04:36 PM||||I close the decklid about a foot, and remove the grills.  The hinges move out of the way enough to get your hands in there.||||reg||1
Z||000008||AL||08-02-2000||08:05 PM||||i get on the right side of the car and remove spark plugs 1&3 then i go to the left and remove 6 and i then install the new one's takes me 5 minutes and i don't remove nothing.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Gold-86SE||08-02-2000||08:07 PM||||<BR>I vote for deck lid removal, anybody who watches my posts, knows that I say this all the time.<P>Definately my preferred method for any work on the back of the engine.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000010||AL||08-03-2000||12:11 AM||||i meant 5 plug, not 6.||||reg||1
Z||000011||-=shame=-||08-04-2000||07:54 AM||||Or, you could invest in a two foot midget with three foot arms. Man they come in very helpful in just about any situation.<P>Just a joke PC police.||||reg||6
